<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chōsokabe Nobuchika</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1565">1565</a>–<a href="/years/1587">1587</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Chosokabe Nobuchika</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chōsokabe Nobuchika (1565–1587) was the eldest son and heir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chosokabe-motochika">Chōsokabe Motochika</a>. Sent with his father to support <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a>'s invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a> against the Shimazu, he was killed at the Battle of Hetsugigawa in the winter of 1586–87. His death led to a bitter succession dispute in which Motochika chose his younger son Morichika as heir.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chosokabe-nobuchika.jpg" alt="Chōsokabe Nobuchika" width="320" height="431" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Utagawa Yoshiiku · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ch%C5%8Dsokabe_Nobuchika.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
